{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs Java 6 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following Java 6 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nLittle Petya loves training spiders. Petya has a board n\u2009\u00d7\u2009m in size. Each cell of the board initially has a spider sitting on it. After one second Petya chooses a certain action for each spider, and all of them humbly perform its commands. There are 5 possible commands: to stay idle or to move from current cell to some of the four side-neighboring cells (that is, one command for each of the four possible directions). Petya gives the commands so that no spider leaves the field. It is allowed for spiders to pass through each other when they crawl towards each other in opposite directions. All spiders crawl simultaneously and several spiders may end up in one cell. Petya wants to know the maximum possible number of spider-free cells after one second.\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the Java 6 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class ProblemE {\n    static int N, M;\n    static final int BIG = 9999999;\n    static Set<Integer> options = new HashSet<Integer>();\n    \n    static void search(int idx, int level, int pattern) {\n        if (idx >= N) {\n            options.add(pattern);\n            return;\n        }\n        if (level >= 1) {\n            search(idx+1, level, pattern|(1<<idx));\n        }\n        if (level <= M - 2) {\n            search(idx+1, level, pattern|(1<<(idx+N*2)));\n        }\n        if (idx >= 1) {\n            search(idx+1, level, pattern|(1<<((idx-1)+N)));\n        }\n        if (idx <= N - 2) {\n            search(idx+1, level, pattern|(1<<((idx+1)+N)));\n        }\n        search(idx+1, level, pattern|(1<<(idx+N)));\n    }\n    \n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        String[] tokens = in.readLine().trim().split(\"\\\\s+\");\n        N = Integer.parseInt(tokens[0]);\n        M = Integer.parseInt(tokens[1]);\n        if (N > M) {\n            int temp = N;\n            N = M;\n            M = temp;\n        }\n    \n        int[][] cache = new int[M+1][1<<(N*3)];\n        for (int i = 0 ; i <= M ; i++) {\n            Arrays.fill(cache[i], BIG);\n        }\n        cache[0][0] = 0;\n        \n        for (int k = 0 ; k < M ; k++) {\n            options.clear();\n            search(0, k, 0);\n            for (int s = 0 ; s < 1<<(N*2) ; s++) {\n                if (cache[k][s] != BIG) {\n                    for (int opt : options) {\n                        int combined = (opt | s);\n                        int nextS = combined >> N;\n                        int cost = Integer.bitCount(combined & ((1<<N) - 1));\n                        cache[k+1][nextS] = Math.min(cache[k+1][nextS], cache[k][s] + cost);\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        \n        int best = BIG;\n        for (int t = 0 ; t < 1<<(N*2) ; t++) {\n            best = Math.min(best, cache[M][t] + Integer.bitCount(t));\n        }\n        System.out.println(M * N - best);\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class ProblemE {\n    static int N, M;\n    static final int BIG = 9999999;\n    static List<Integer> options = new ArrayList<Integer>();\n    \n    static void search(int idx, int pattern) {\n        if (idx >= N) {\n            options.add(pattern);\n            return;\n        }\n        // Option 1: stay in place (command N)\n        search(idx+1, pattern | (1 << (idx + N)));\n        // Option 2: move up (command 0)\n        if (idx >= 1) {\n            search(idx+1, pattern | (1 << (idx - 1)));\n        } else {\n            // if at top row, can only stay (cannot move up)\n            search(idx+1, pattern | (1 << (idx + N)));\n        }\n        // Option 3: move down (command 1)\n        if (idx <= N - 2) {\n            search(idx+1, pattern | (1 << (idx + 1 + N)));\n        } else {\n            // if at bottom row, can only stay (cannot move down)\n            search(idx+1, pattern | (1 << (idx + N)));\n        }\n        // Option 4: move left (command 2)\n        if (idx >= 1) {\n            search(idx+1, pattern | (1 << (idx - 1 + N)));\n        } else {\n            // if at leftmost column, can only stay (cannot move left)\n            search(idx+1, pattern | (1 << (idx + N)));\n        }\n        // Option 5: move right (command 3)\n        if (idx <= N - 2) {\n            search(idx+1, pattern | (1 << (idx + 1)));\n        } else {\n            // if at rightmost column, can only stay (cannot move right)\n            search(idx+1, pattern | (1 << (idx + N)));\n        }\n    }\n    \n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        String[] tokens = in.readLine().trim().split(\"\\\\s+\");\n        N = Integer.parseInt(tokens[0]);\n        M = Integer.parseInt(tokens[1]);\n        \n        // Make N the smaller dimension for optimization\n        if (N > M) {\n            int temp = N;\n            N = M;\n            M = temp;\n        }\n    \n        // dp[k][mask] = minimum number of occupied cells after k columns\n        int[][] dp = new int[M+1][1 << (N*2)];\n        for (int i = 0; i <= M; i++) {\n            Arrays.fill(dp[i], BIG);\n        }\n        dp[0][0] = 0;\n        \n        for (int col = 0; col < M; col++) {\n            options.clear();\n            search(0, 0);\n            \n            for (int mask = 0; mask < (1 << (N*2)); mask++) {\n                if (dp[col][mask] == BIG) continue;\n                \n                for (int opt : options) {\n                    // mask represents which cells are occupied in current column configuration\n                    // opt represents where spiders from current column move to\n                    // We need to compute which cells will be occupied in the next state\n                    \n                    // Extract current column's occupied cells (lower N bits)\n                    int currentOccupied = mask & ((1 << N) - 1);\n                    // Extract next column's occupied cells (upper N bits)\n                    int nextOccupied = mask >> N;\n                    \n                    // Calculate where spiders from current column go\n                    int targetMask = opt;\n                    \n                    // The new state for next column will be:\n                    // - spiders coming from current column (targetMask)\n                    // - plus what was already in next column (nextOccupied)\n                    int newNextOccupied = nextOccupied | (targetMask >> N);\n                    \n                    // Calculate cost: number of spiders that end up in current column\n                    // (i.e., spiders that move to positions in current column)\n                    int cost = Integer.bitCount(targetMask & ((1 << N) - 1));\n                    \n                    int newMask = (newNextOccupied << N) | targetMask;\n                    dp[col+1][newMask] = Math.min(dp[col+1][newMask], dp[col][mask] + cost);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        \n        int best = BIG;\n        for (int mask = 0; mask < (1 << (N*2)); mask++) {\n            if (dp[M][mask] != BIG) {\n                best = Math.min(best, dp[M][mask] + Integer.bitCount(mask >> N));\n            }\n        }\n        \n        System.out.println(N * M - best);\n    }\n}\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.3\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-3.576278118089249e-07, -5.602679812000133e-05, -1.0728830375228426e-06, 0.0, -2.0503786799963564e-05, -1.2874520507466514e-05, -1.6689160474925302e-05, -3.933898824470816e-06, -5.8412379075889476e-06, -1.0847986231965479e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.6689160474925302e-05, -4.768360213347478e-06, -1.2397689715726301e-05, -0.00010430268594063818, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -4.017272294731811e-05, -0.0002964295563288033, -0.0007121411035768688, -2.50339189733495e-06, -9.298280929215252e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.0013266343157738447, -0.12693938612937927, -3.2186455882765586e-06, -0.007952101528644562, -8.344646857949556e-07, -0.03379283845424652, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.3232143828645349e-05, -0.002476722002029419, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -4.756337511935271e-05, -0.0008117241668514907, -9.989239333663136e-05, -0.029754582792520523, -8.4638240878121e-06, -0.2835703194141388, -0.00045468006283044815, -0.01827263832092285, -0.19252130389213562, -0.03433631733059883, -3.2186455882765586e-06, -4.482168878894299e-05, -2.0146166207268834e-05, -1.4066597032069694e-05, -0.0004318020073696971, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -4.291525328881107e-06, -7.116541382856667e-05, -0.026490624994039536, -0.00018404220463708043, -0.0002520958660170436, -2.753696753643453e-05, -0.00019894051365554333, -0.3383074700832367, -0.0755319744348526, 0.0, -5.364403477869928e-06, -5